To prepare the champagne risotto, place @butter{2%tbsp} in a #saucepan{}, add the @onion{1%small}(finely chopped) and let it turn golden; sprinkle in the @Carnaroli rice{1 ¾%cup} and toast it for a few moments over high heat, stirring with a #wooden spoon{}.

Then pour all the @Champagne{3%glasses} into the saucepan; stir the rice continuously so that it doesn't stick to the bottom and if necessary, add a few ladles of @vegetable broth{2%cups} to finish cooking.

A few moments before the end of cooking, turn off the heat and stir in the remaining @butter{1 ½%tbsp} and the @Grana Padano PDO cheese{3.5%oz}(grated).

Serve the champagne risotto while still hot, accompanied by a flute of the same champagne used for cooking.